{"url": "https://www.monash.edu/admissions/english-language-requirements", "final_url": "https://www.monash.edu/admissions/entry-requirements/english-language", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-10-30", "text": "Skip to content\nSkip to navigation\nHome\nMonash Australia\nMonash Australia\nMonash India\nMonash Indonesia\nMonash Malaysia\nMonash Prato\nMonash Suzhou\nMonash Boston Hub\nMonash Australia\nCourses\nMonash Online\nLibrary\nDonate\nSTAFF\nStaff\nStaff portal\nIntranet\nM-Space\nThe Insider\nSTAFF\nSTUDENTS\nStudents\nStudent portal\nStudent website\nMonash Connect\nMonash Online hub\nSTUDENTS\nALUMNI\nAlumni\nAlumni portal\nAlumni website\nALUMNI\nSEARCH\nADMISSIONS\nHOW TO APPLY\nENTRY REQUIREMENTS\nAPPLY FOR CREDIT\nSTUDY OPTIONS\nMORE\nAPPLY TO STUDY\nEntry requirements\nMinimum entry requirements\nAustralian Tertiary Admission Rank (ATAR)\nEnglish language requirements\nEnglish-speaking countries\nAge requirements for admission\nEntry-level requirements for graduate courses\nNew Zealand NCEA\nChina Gaokao\nExtra requirements for courses\nChecks\nCertifying documents\nAdmission and aptitude tests\nSupplementary VTAC information\nGenuine student requirement\nYou are here:\nHome | Entry requirements | English language requirements\nEnglish language requirements\nEnglish is the language of instruction at Monash University. You need to demonstrate that you have a level of English which will allow you to engage fully in your education.\nAs well as meeting the minimum English language requirements, some courses have higher requirements. To find this information, check the Entry Requirements section for your preferred course in our find a course page.\nInternational students applying to Monash must also meet the English language visa requirements set by the Department of Home Affairs, as these requirements differ from Monash.\nMonash University does not accept competency-based qualifications or subjects as evidence of meeting English language requirements.\nThe English language requirements you must meet depend on your educational background.\nENGLISH-SPEAKING BACKGROUND\nNON-ENGLISH-SPEAKING BACKGROUND\nIf you\u2019ve completed six years of schooling at an English medium institution in an English-speaking country (including Australia) before the age of 19, you can meet the English language requirements in one of the following ways.\nSecondary schooling\nTertiary study (including VET and higher education)\nEnglish test\nMonash English\nInternational students who do not meet the English language requirement based on their English test results (but meet all other entry requirements) may want to consider completing Monash English.\nDomestic students who have not satisfied the English language requirements (but meet all other entry requirements) will require approval from the dean of the degree faculty (or nominee) to complete Monash English.\nOther study programs at Monash\nSingle units and non-award study\nTo enrol in single units or a non-award study program (including exchange and study abroad), you must meet the University's minimum English language requirements; see: 3.4 \u2013 Minimum English language requirements for entry to Monash courses and units (pdf, 0.58 mb).\nApproved non-award enabling programs\nFor minimum English language requirements for approved enabling programs, see: 3.5 \u2013 Minimum English language requirements for non-award enabling programs (pdf, 0.58 mb).\nProcedure\nFor more information on English language requirements, please refer to the Admission to Coursework Courses and Units Procedure 3: Minimum English language requirements (pdf, 0.58 mb).\nGot a question? Message Monash Connect\nTry MoVA, Monash's virtual assistant\nMoVA has answers to most common questions. If it can't find an answer, it can connect you with a real person using messaging or help you make an online enquiry.\nMonash College and University diploma enquiries\nIf you're studying a diploma at Monash University or any course at College, please make your enquiry through Monash College.\nWe acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians\nCOMMUNITY\nFaculties\nLocations\nDiversity and inclusion\nSafety and security\nSustainability\nRESOURCES\nImportant dates\nHow to apply\nA-Z index\nPolicy Bank\nFAQs\nCONTACT\nContact us\nCampus maps\nJobs at Monash\nRecruit a student\nPay online\nNEWS\nLatest news\nMonash Lens\nPodcasts\nA Different Lens\nMonash Life\nON OUR SITE\nWho we are\nFind a course\nFind a researcher\nPartner with Monash\nSitemap\nREGISTERED AUSTRALIAN UNIVERSITY\nABN: 12 377 614 012\nTEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140\nCRICOS PROVIDER NUMBER\nMonash University: 00008C\nMonash College: 01857J\nAUTHORISED BY\nExecutive Director, Marketing\nWebsite feedback\nLast updated: Apr 2026\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer & copyright\nTerms & conditions\nData privacy & cyber security\nData Consent Settings\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Monash University\nWe use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions\nAccept all\nCookie settings", "links": [["Home", "https://www.monash.edu/admissions"], ["Courses", "https://www.monash.edu/study/courses"], ["Monash Online", "https://online.monash.edu/"], ["Library", "https://www.monash.edu/library"], ["Donate", "https://www.monash.edu/giving"], ["Admissions", "https://www.monash.edu/admissions"], ["How to apply", "https://www.monash.edu/admissions/apply"], ["How to apply", "https://www.monash.edu/admissions/apply"], ["Undergraduate domestic", "https://www.monash.edu/admissions/apply/domestic-ug"], ["Honours domestic", "https://www.monash.edu/admissions/apply/domestic-honours"], ["Graduate domestic", "https://www.monash.edu/admissions/apply/domestic-pg"], ["Undergraduate international", "https://www.monash.edu/admissions/apply/